content.text:
Now game.js integration. Add imports, constants, constructor boss, run fields, cleanup, update logic, methods.

Constants:
```
import { Boss }...
const FIRST_BOSS = 700;
const BOSS_INTERVAL = 900;
const BOSS_NAMES = [...]
```
Run:
```
nextBoss: FIRST_BOSS,
bosses:0,
creditedBosses:0,
bossKills? use bosses.
```
startRun: boss despawn, bossFight null, UI hide.
goHome same.
update(mode over/paused) boss update? If boss active paused, keep visual hover: call `this.boss.update(dt*0.3...)` maybe in update branch. But game paused by overlay, boss frozen is fine. During 'over', boss despawned. During perk boss can't. So skip.

updateRunning:
- `const inBattle = !!run.battle || !!run.bossFight;`
- `scheduleSpawns()` guard.
- after enemy/battle section, boss approach logic; startBossFight.
- milestone check add `!this.boss.active`.
- If bossFight, updateBossFight and return? We still need updateCamera at end. updateBossFight handles camera via updateCamera called after. Do:
```
if (run.bossFight) {
  this.updateBossFight(dt);
  if (this.mode !== 'running') return;
} else if (this.boss.active) {
  this.boss.update(dt,this.time, run.speed);
  if (this.boss.z >= -10.6) this.startBossFight();
} else { maybe spawnBoss check }
```
Order: boss spawn check should occur before boss.update? Put:
```
if (!run.battle && !run.bossFight && !this.boss.active && run.distance >= run.nextBoss - 120 && !this.enemy.active) this.spawnBoss();
if (run.bossFight) updateBossFight
else if (this.boss.active) { update; if z>=-10.6 startBossFight }
else if (run.battle) ...
else if enemy...
```
But enemy update block currently handles battle. Need restructure carefully while preserving.

Current structure:
```
if (run.battle) { updateBattle; ... }
else if (this.enemy.active) { approach; startBattle; }

// milestone
if (!run.battle && ... )
updateCamera
```

We add boss before milestone:
```
// boss spawn check (only if no battle/enemy/boss)
if (!run.battle && !run.bossFight && !this.boss.active && !this.enemy.active && run.distance >= run.nextBoss - 120) this.spawnBoss();

if (run.bossFight) { this.updateBossFight(dt); if mode!==running return; }
else if (this.boss.active) {
  this.boss.targetX = clamp(this.player.x*0.35, -3,3) etc;
  this.boss.update(dt,this.time,run.speed);
  if (this.boss.z >= -10.6) this.startBossFight();
}
```
But boss approach should not update while normal fight (no battle since spawn condition). Fine. Note scroll during approach continues at full speed; boss.update adds speed+14 (scroll ~ run.speed). So closure = 2*scroll+14? I pass `run.speed` and boss adds speed+14 where speed param is run.speed, but boss.z already moves with world? Boss is separate, so yes boss closes at 2x. I passed speed=run.speed; good but maybe too fast: at speed 20 closure 54 m/s, 109m gap in 2s. Dramatic. Use `run.speed*0.55` in call to closure 25 m/s = 4.4s. Actually boss.z increases by speed+14; pass 0.55*speed. Fine. Or set boss approach speed internal fixed 14 and pass scroll? We want relative closure. Simpler: `this.boss.update(dt, this.time, run.speed*0.7)` → closure ~28. good.

During boss approach, player still collides with entities. Fine.

`inBattle` should be set before. If boss.active but not fight, inBattle false → collisions continue. Good.

scheduleSpawns guard:
```
if (!this.run || this.boss.active || this.run.bossFight) return;
```
But at startRun scheduleSpawns called after boss reset.

spawnBoss:
```
const run=this.run;
const tier=run.bosses; // count defeated, 0-based
const name = BOSS_NAMES[tier % len] + (tier >= len ? ` ${roman(tier)}` : '');
const hp = Math.round((780 + tier*620) * (1 + Math.min(.5, run.distance/12000)));
run.nextBoss = Math.max(run.nextBoss, Math.floor(run.distance)+260);? No keep.
this.boss.spawn(0,-125,{tier,name,maxHp:hp});
run.bossFight=null;
this.nextSpawnDistance = Math.max(this.nextSpawnDistance, run.nextBoss + 40);
clear hazards/gates ahead
ui.showBossWarning(name);
audio.bossWarn();
ui.toast('BOSS INCOMING','bad', 1800)? warning already. Skip toast maybe.
```
`this.nextSpawnDistance` currently absolute distance. At distance 580, spawn ahead maybe 720. set to max(..., nextBoss+30=730). fine.
Remove entities ahead:
```
for (const ent of this.entities) {
 if (['gate','saw','laser'].includes(ent.kind) && ent.z < -18) this.removeEntity(ent);
}
```
Gate group removal uses scene.remove. Fine.
Boss x = player.x? spawn at 0.

Boss name roman helper; simple suffix `MK ${tier+1}` after cycle. Use `BOSS_NAMES[tier % 5] + (tier >=5 ? ' MK ' + (Math.floor(tier/5)+1) : '')`. Fine.

startBossFight:
```
const run=this.run, boss=this.boss;
const b={
 name: boss.name, tier: boss.tier,
 maxHp: boss.maxHp, hp: boss.maxHp,
 startCount: run.count, elapsed:0,
 attackTimer: 1.7, telegraph:null,
 phase:1, spark:0, hudTimer:0,
 startPlayer: run.count
};
run.bossFight=b; this.bossFight=b;
boss.z=-10.6; boss.targetX=this.player.x*0.3;
ui.showBoss(...); ui.hideSteerHint(); audio.clash(); addShake; burst; shock; toast maybe `${name} — DESTROY IT` 'bad'
```
Also hide battle? not visible.

updateBossFight:
```
const b=run.bossFight,e=this.boss; if(!b) return;
b.elapsed+=dt;
const frac=b.hp/b.maxHp;
let phase=frac>0.66?1:frac>0.33?2:3;
if(phase>b.phase){b.phase=phase; e.setPhase(phase); e.setHpFraction(frac); ui.updateBoss...; ui.toast(`PHASE ${phase}`,'bad',1200); audio.bossWarn(); addShake(.5); }
e.setHpFraction(frac);
e.targetX=clamp(this.player.x*0.35,-3,3);
// DPS
const dps=this.bossPlayerDps();
b.hp=Math.max(0,b.hp-dps*dt);
// attack
if(b.telegraph){
  b.telegraph.t -= dt;
  if(b.telegraph.t<=0){ this.resolveBossSlam(b); }
} else {
  b.attackTimer-=dt;
  if(b.attackTimer<=0) {
     b.telegraph={x:this.player.x, t:0.95, radius:2.35, tier:b.tier};
     e.attackAt(b.telegraph.x);
     this.audio...
     b.attackTimer=999 // set after resolve
  }
}
// fx sparks
b.spark-=dt; if(b.spark<=0 && b.hp>0){...}
e.update(dt,this.time,3.5);
// hud throttle
b.hudTimer-=dt; if<=0 { b.hudTimer=.08; ui.updateBoss...}
if(b.hp<=0){this.winBoss(); return;}
if(run.count<=0){this.die(); return;}
```
Note e.hit() flicker on dps? call every .12 when spark.

Boss damage attack:
```
resolveBossSlam(b){
 const e=this.boss;
 b.telegraph=null; e.endAttack();
 const tx=b.slamX? store
 ...
}
```
