Boss active approach: if startBossFight sets bossFight then we return? Good.

Now add boss methods after updateBattle/winBattle maybe before perks. Add spawnBoss, startBossFight, updateBossFight, bossPlayerDps, begin telegraph, resolve, win.

Careful: updateBossFight calls `this.die()` and returns. `run.count` may go 0 via slam; then die called inside resolve; updateBossFight should detect mode. We'll check after resolve.

Implement:

```
spawnBoss() {
 const run=this.run; if(!run) return;
 const tier=run.bosses;
 const cycle=Math.floor(tier/BOSS_NAMES.length);
 const name=BOSS_NAMES[tier%BOSS_NAMES.length]+(cycle?` MK ${cycle+1}`:'');
 const hp=Math.round((800+tier*620)*(1+Math.min(0.6,run.distance/14000)));
 this.boss.spawn(0,-130,{tier,name,maxHp:hp});
 this.boss.name=name;
 run.bossFight=null; this.bossFight=null;
 this.nextSpawnDistance=Math.max(this.nextSpawnDistance, run.nextBoss+40);
 for (const ent of this.entities) {
   if (ent.kind==='gate'||ent.kind==='saw'||ent.kind==='laser') {
     if (ent.z < -24) this.removeEntity(ent);
   }
 }
 this.entities=this.entities.filter...
 this.ui.showBossWarning(name);
 this.audio.bossWarn();
 this.addShake(0.25);
}
```
Note removing while iterating with for...of over array and splicing? removeEntity only sets removed, doesn't splice. Fine.

`startBossFight()`:
```
if (!this.boss.active || run.bossFight) return;
...
this.boss.z=-10.6;
this.boss.targetX=...
this.boss.phase=1; setPhase(1); setHpFraction(1)
b...
this.ui.showBattle? no.
this.ui.showBoss(...)
this.ui.hideSteerHint()
this.audio.clash(); this.addShake(.45)
burst etc
this.ui.toast(`${b.name} — DESTROY IT`,'bad',2200); // warning may still be on; maybe delay. Boss warning lasts 2.45s, approach ~4.5s after spawn, so warning gone.
```
`boss.name` stored.

`updateBossFight`:
- phase determination and UI.
- Dps add.
- hitPulse.
- Attack telegraph starts first after 1.6.
- On begin: `b.telegraph={x:clamp(this.player.x,-TRACK_LIMIT,TRACK_LIMIT),t:0.95,radius:2.35}`; boss.attackAt; audio maybe `this.audio.clash()`? use `bossWarn` too loud. Use `this.audio.slice()`? Better no sound or low tone. Add `this.audio.bossSlam?` only at impact. Use `this.audio.gate(false)` weird. Skip telegraph sound; VFX enough. Could use `this.audio.click()` soft. Let's add `this.audio.slice()` — quick whoosh. Fine.
- `this.boss.update(dt,this.time,2.5)`. During fight boss.z fixed (update only moves if z < -10.6; exactly -10.6 no move).
- Sparks at boss x/z chest: `this.fx.burst(e.x+rand(-1.2,1.2), rand(2,4.5), e.z+0.6, 0xff6a5c, 2, {speed:4, life:.4, gravity:-4})`. Maybe colors phase.
- UI throttle.
- win check first? If hp<=0 and count<=0 same frame, award win (kill) maybe. Do hp first.
- check count 0 after slam only; but count could be 0 from something? During boss collisions disabled. Fine.

`resolveBossSlam(b)`:
```
const t=b.telegraph; b.telegraph=null; this.boss.endAttack();
const hit=Math.abs(this.player.x-t.x)<=t.radius;
this.shock.ring(t.x,0.7,0.5,0xff2f4e,{scale:1.4,life:.5,growth:12});
this.fx.burst(t.x,1.0,0.4,0xff2f4e,20,{speed:6,spread:1.4,life:.7,gravity:-8});
if (hit) {
  if (run.powers.shield>0) { floater 'BLOCKED'; addShake .25; audio.shield(); }
  else {
    const dmg=...;
    this.floaters.float(`-${dmg}`,this.player.x,3.2,0.6,'#ff9db0',{...});
    this.damagePlayer(dmg,new THREE.Vector3(t.x,1,0.4),'boss');
    this.addShake(.55); this.audio.bossSlam();
  }
} else {
  floater 'DODGE' etc; audio.slice; this.shock.ring(... cyan)
}
b.attackTimer = max(1.35, 2.9 - (b.phase-1)*.5 - b.tier*.05);
```
But damagePlayer sets count and may call die; then b.attackTimer set okay.
- `damagePlayer` also sets `ui.flash('hit')`, audio hit. Additionally bossSlam sound maybe overlapping. Fine.

`winBoss`:
```
const run=this.run, b=run.bossFight, e=this.boss;
...
run.bossFight=null; this.bossFight=null;
